.TH XD\-PRIVACY 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-privacy \- Privacy Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-privacy
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-privacy
is the Privacy applet (Control Panel > User Accounts):
.TP
.B General
Whether programs and the Start menus list your recently opened documents,
for how long, and Clear List; and emptying old items from the Recycle Bin
and old temporary files automatically.
.TP
.B Location
Whether programs may use your location, and the programs that asked, with
Allow, Deny and Remove.
.TP
.B Program Permissions
What programs were allowed or refused through the desktop portals (camera,
microphone, speakers, notifications, running in the background,
screenshots, the desktop background, location), per program, with Allow,
Deny and Remove.
A removed answer makes the program ask again.
.PP
The settings are GNOME's
.RB ( org.gnome.desktop.privacy
and
.BR org.gnome.system.location ),
which GTK, xdg-desktop-portal and GeoClue already honour.
.BR xd\-shell (1)
honours the recent documents settings in its Start menus and jump lists,
and once a day deletes the Recycle Bin's items deleted longer ago than the
chosen number of days (by their deletion date) and the user's own
temporary files in
.B $TMPDIR
untouched for as long.
Answers given to programs are kept in xdg-desktop-portal's permission store
.RB ( org.freedesktop.impl.portal.PermissionStore ),
and changes to them take effect at once.
Finding the location needs GeoClue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.I n
(0: General, 1: Location, 2: Program Permissions).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-control (1),
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xdg\-desktop\-portal (1)
